## 💡 Pro Tips for Jury

### Talking Points to Always Include
- "Full-stack implementation"
- "Modern Angular 21"
- "Secure authentication (JWT)"
- "Event-driven notifications"
- "Scalable architecture"
- "SOLID principles"
- "Type-safe with TypeScript"
- "Comprehensive testing"

### What Impresses Jury
✅ **Understanding the "why"** - "We chose this because..."
✅ **Trade-offs awareness** - "This approach gives us X but costs Y"
✅ **Real-world thinking** - "For production, we would..."
✅ **Code quality** - "Our service layer ensures..."
✅ **Security first** - "We validate at every layer"
✅ **User perspective** - "This feature improves user experience by..."

### What to Avoid
❌ Just describing what code does
❌ Not knowing why you made a decision
❌ Overpromising on features not implemented
❌ Blaming external factors
❌ Not listening to questions
❌ Getting defensive about feedback

